{
  "id": "EDU102",
  "title": "The Contact Plan Has an Offline Copy",
  "family": "learning",
  "category": "public safety/preparedness",
  "premise": "A household wants to reconnect during a disruption, but its fictional contact plan exists only on an unavailable device. A reviewed preparedness example adds an accessible offline copy and a mutually agreed contact procedure.",
  "hook": "What if the plan is inside the phone that will not turn on?",
  "visible_action": "A phone screen darkens while a simplified, privacy-protected contact card remains visible in a designated kit slot.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "A preparedness plan should account for loss of its usual communication tools.",
  "gate": "Use fake contact details; obtain current official guidance and household consent before any real plan. Do not ask viewers to guess an emergency response or choose an action in a simulated emergency; any response content must come from reviewed official guidance.",
